<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Mountain View Loop (from Maxwell Sno-Park)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:237-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.460958" lon="-121.976421"><ele>1129.3</ele><name>Maxwell Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:maxwell-sno-park (OSM parking way/319966868, Maxwell Butte Sno Park); confidence: high; pdf_page: 236; book_elev_ft: 3690; quote: map 50: C (Maxwell) 3690'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.470640" lon="-121.977290"><ele>1167.6</ele><name>Loop junction (south tip of the loop)</name><desc>source: south vertex of USFS SNO-4176 Outer Mountain View Loop where Flat Loop SNO-4182 meets it, about 0.7 mi from the sno-park by SNO-4181/4182; confidence: high; pdf_page: 238; quote: The trail at 0.7 mile then meets the Mountain View Loop for the first time</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.477980" lon="-121.957730"><ele>1320.2</ele><name>Maxwell Cutoff junction (east end of Shelter View Ridge)</name><desc>source: junction of SNO-4176 and SNO-4185 West Side Cutoff (the book's Maxwell Cutoff Trail); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 239; quote: ski east on the ridge to the forest, actually the boundary of the Mount Jefferson Wilderness, then turn north on a road to continue on the loop. Turning south puts you on the Maxwell Cutoff Trail.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.485340" lon="-121.948850"><ele>1293.6</ele><name>North-east corner of the loop</name><desc>source: east end of USFS SNO-4176 (start/end vertex of its ring); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 236</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.489780" lon="-121.988460"><ele>1114.7</ele><name>Fay Lake Trail Y-junction</name><desc>source: where SNO-4175 Fay Lake Trail touches SNO-4176 on the north-west; confidence: high; pdf_page: 239; quote: Near the west foot of the loop's north leg you will be near the Y-junction of the Fay Lake Trail.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.470640" lon="-121.977290"><ele>1167.6</ele><name>Loop junction (south tip of the loop)</name><desc>source: loop closes; confidence: high; pdf_page: 238; quote: it eventually turns south near the highway, which it will parallel through continuous clearcuts</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.460958" lon="-121.976421"><ele>1129.3</ele><name>Maxwell Sno-Park (finish)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high; pdf_page: 236; book_elev_ft: 3690</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Mountain View Loop (from Maxwell Sno-Park)</name><desc>1. Maxwell Sno-Park -&gt; Loop junction (south tip of the loop): usfs-trail (medium), 0.86 mi | 2. Loop junction (south tip of the loop) -&gt; Maxwell Cutoff junction (east end of Shelter View Ridge): usfs-trail (high), 1.31 mi | 3. Maxwell Cutoff junction (east end of Shelter View Ridge) -&gt; North-east corner of the loop: usfs-trail (high), 0.82 mi | 4. North-east corner of the loop -&gt; Fay Lake Trail Y-junction: usfs-trail (high), 2.34 mi | 5. Fay Lake Trail Y-junction -&gt; Loop junction (south tip of the loop): usfs-trail (high), 2.10 mi | 6. Loop junction (south tip of the loop) -&gt; Maxwell Sno-Park (finish): usfs-trail (medium), 0.86 mi</desc>
